  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) Early Action intervention to expected floods in Unity and Upper Nile States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peace and security remain elusive in South Sudan as conflict, insecurity, and natural hazards continue to be the main drivers of humanitarian needs in the country. Although intercommunal conflicts, sub-national violence, and pockets of crime are still being recorded and contribute to displacement, climate shocks such as drought and flooding have become more chronic and have impacted people severely over the last four years. 
 
This project aims to maintain smooth access in Bentiu internally displaced persons (IDP) camp and Malakal Protection of Civilian (POC) sites to ensure flood-affected population lives in a safe and dignified environment. This is being achieved through drainage cleaning to remove silt from storm water channels and culverts, grading and compacting access roads as well as rehabilitation and routine maintenance of the berm and dykes. Further, IOM is engaging communities to enhance resilience and ownership of flood mitigation infrastructures.</narrative>
  </description>
